2. PHASE 4C PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Build a comprehensive Universal DOM Scanner.

The scanner must discover interactive and potentially interactive website elements across different website structures and frameworks.

It must support:

1. Standard HTML form controls.
2. Contenteditable elements.
3. ARIA-based interactive controls.
4. Custom dropdowns and listboxes.
5. Date and time controls.
6. Radio buttons and checkboxes.
7. Select elements.
8. Open Shadow DOM.
9. Accessible same-origin iframes.
10. Dynamically inserted elements.
11. Long pages and large forms.
12. Off-screen elements.
13. Elements loaded after scrolling or user interaction.
14. Elements with dynamically changing attributes.
15. Modern JavaScript-generated interfaces.

The scanner must work deterministically using browser APIs and locally executed JavaScript.

No external AI API must be required.

The scanner is a discovery system, not an automatic interaction or security-bypass system.

