6. OPEN SHADOW DOM SUPPORT

Modern websites frequently use Web Components.

Implement recursive discovery through accessible open Shadow DOM.

Requirements:

1. Detect elements with shadowRoot.
2. Traverse open shadow roots recursively.
3. Discover interactive descendants.
4. Preserve host-to-shadow relationships.
5. Generate locators that can identify the element within its shadow host chain.
6. Support nested open Shadow DOM.
7. Deduplicate elements discovered through multiple paths.

A locator may need to represent a chain such as:

Document
→ Shadow Host A
→ Shadow Root A
→ Shadow Host B
→ Shadow Root B
→ Target Element

Do not assume a normal document.querySelector() can reach elements inside Shadow DOM.

Do not claim support for closed Shadow DOM.

Closed Shadow DOM must be reported as inaccessible when its contents cannot be inspected through supported browser APIs.

Do not attempt to bypass encapsulation.

