7. SAME-ORIGIN IFRAME SUPPORT

Implement recursive scanning of accessible same-origin iframes.

Requirements:

- Discover iframe elements.
- Inspect accessible iframe documents.
- Recursively scan same-origin iframe content.
- Maintain the iframe hierarchy.
- Preserve frame URL and origin metadata.
- Generate frame-aware locators.
- Deduplicate results.
- Handle unloaded frames.
- Handle navigation during scanning.
- Handle detached iframe documents.
- Handle cross-origin access restrictions safely.

For cross-origin iframes:

- Detect the iframe.
- Record that it contains inaccessible content.
- Do not attempt to bypass the same-origin policy.
- Do not inject unauthorized scripts into cross-origin frames.

All discovered iframe content must remain subject to the existing origin and session security architecture.

Important credential rule

Phase 4B credential filling must not be weakened.

Credential filling must remain restricted to the exact authorized top-level origin and approved target context.

Do not use iframe scanning to bypass credential origin restrictions.

