13. PRIVACY AND SENSITIVE ELEMENT HANDLING

The scanner must preserve all Phase 4B protections.

Password fields

For input[type=password]:

- Detect the element.
- Record its type.
- Record its accessible label.
- Record its locator.
- Record its origin and structural context.
- Never capture its value.
- Never serialize its value.
- Never include it in logs.
- Never include it in screenshots or diagnostic output.

Password fields should be classified as credential-capable controls.

They must not automatically create vault entries.

Other sensitive fields

Handle cautiously:

- Credit card fields.
- CVV fields.
- Bank account fields.
- Payment-related controls.
- OTP fields.
- One-time authentication fields.
- Security-question fields.
- Personal identification fields.

The scanner may discover their structural metadata, but must not automatically collect or persist sensitive values.

Do not bypass CAPTCHA, MFA, authentication challenges, or website security mechanisms.

Do not automatically submit sensitive forms.

